# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in your own values.
# `.env` is git-ignored. `.env.example` is committed — never put a real token here.

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# GITHUB_TOKEN  (optional, but strongly recommended)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Without a token : 60  API requests per hour  (~6 scans)
# With a token    : 5,000 API requests per hour (~500 scans)
#
# Create one at https://github.com/settings/tokens
#
# Scopes needed:
#   Public repositories only → NONE. Leave every checkbox unchecked.
#   Private repositories     → `repo` (classic) or Contents:read (fine-grained).
#
# Security rules, in order of how often they are broken:
#   1. Never commit a token.
#   2. Never paste one into a chat, an issue, or a screenshot.
#   3. Grant the narrowest scope that works, and set an expiry date.
#   4. If a token is ever exposed, revoke it immediately — do not "keep an eye
#      on it". GitHub scans public content and auto-revokes tokens it finds,
#      but a token can be harvested by a bot long before that happens.
#
GITHUB_TOKEN=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Optional settings
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# GitHub Enterprise Server API root. Leave unset for github.com.
# GITHUB_API_BASE=https://github.example.com/api/v3

# Disable coloured output. Any non-empty value works. See https://no-color.org
# NO_COLOR=1

# Print stack traces on error.
# DEBUG=1
